2. Definitions

   "Licensor" is Love Wins Media, Inc.

   "Software" is the source code, object code, documentation and other files
   distributed with this license, in the form the Licensor distributes them.

   "You" is the individual or entity exercising rights under this license,
   together with every organization that controls, is controlled by, or is
   under common control with it ("Your company").

   "Hosted Service" is the AudienceKit platform (its API, endpoints and
   services) when operated by the Licensor or on the Licensor's behalf,
   including at audiencekit.com and its subdomains, at the domains of the
   audiences it serves, and in any development, staging or test instance the
   Licensor provides for building against it.

   "Permitted Application" is an application, website, service, script or
   tool that uses the Software, or a Modification, only to connect to the
   Hosted Service.

   "Modification" is any work that is based on the Software or any part of it:
   a changed, translated, ported or otherwise altered version, and any work
   that includes or reproduces the Software or a substantial part of it, in
   source or binary form. An application that only calls, links or depends on
   the Software, without changing it, is not a Modification, but Sections 4 to
   7 apply to its use of the Software.

   "Audience Credential" is an audience ID, API key, access token, client ID
   or similar credential that the Licensor issues.

